{"name":"American Thanksgiving","title":"American Thanksgiving","revision":230358,"url":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/American_Thanksgiving","retrieved":"2026-09-06","license":"CC BY-SA","licenseUrl":"https://www.fandom.com/licensing","language":"en","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Because of the highly established traditions, Thanksgiving has a certain set of expected visuals, including decorations put out by retailers, expected foods to eat, and associations with Autumn."},{"kind":"heading","text":"History"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"The origin of the holiday is the Plymouth Colony learning how to catch eels and grow corn, as well as receiving food, from surrounding Natives hoping to develop alliances. After the tradition was settled, Abraham Lincoln made the day a national holiday, and Americans continue to celebrate the holiday today."},{"kind":"heading","text":"Visuals"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Under Construction"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Media"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Music"},{"kind":"list","text":"\"Thank You for the Music\" by ABBA"},{"kind":"list","text":"\"Thanksgiving Song\" by Mary Chapin Carpenter"},{"kind":"list","text":"\"Thanksgiving Theme\" by Vince Guaraldi Trio (from A Charlie Brown Thanksgiving)"},{"kind":"list","text":"\"Thanksgiving\" by George Winston"},{"kind":"list","text":"\"Alice's Restaurant Massacree\" by Arlo Guthrie"},{"kind":"list","text":"\"Thankful\" by Kelly Clarkson"},{"kind":"list","text":"\"Family Affair\" by Sly & The Family Stone"},{"kind":"list","text":"\"Sweet Potato Pie\" by Ray Charles"},{"kind":"list","text":"\"Harvest Moon\" by Neil Young"},{"kind":"list","text":"\"We Gather Together\" (traditional hymn)"},{"kind":"list","text":"\"Thanksgiving Day\" by Ray Davies"},{"kind":"list","text":"\"Thanksgiving Song\" by Johnny Cash"},{"kind":"list","text":"\"Gratitude\" by Earth, Wind & Fire"},{"kind":"list","text":"\"Thanksgiving\" by Jonathan Coulton"},{"kind":"list","text":"\"Thanksgiving Moon\" by Wayn